⍝ lib/galois.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 19: Galois theory: Galois groups of polynomials over ℚ, cyclotomy, Frobenius
⍝ A Galois group is a permutation group of the roots, in the representation of lib/group.imo (the sorted list of its elements, each a
⍝ permutation of the points 0, 1, …, d − 1 as the list of images).  The roots of a polynomial are numbered by blocks: the roots of the
⍝ linear factors first, then the roots of the other irreducible factors in order of increasing degree; the group is determined up to
⍝ a relabelling of the roots inside the blocks.  Helpers end in _gl.
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 1. cyclotomy and finite fields
unitgroup ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the group (ℤ/n)× of the units of ℤ/n under multiplication, as a permutation group (Cayley's regular representation of the units of zunits(n)); it is also the Galois group of ℚ(ζₙ) over ℚ
unitgroup ξ ≔ (regular (zunits ξ) (a b ↦ (mulmod a b ξ)))
galoiscyclotomic ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the Galois group Gal(ℚ(ζₙ)/ℚ) ≅ (ℤ/n)×, of order φ(n): σₐ(ζ) = ζᵃ for a coprime to n, acting regularly on the primitive n-th roots of unity (the points of the group are the units of ℤ/n in increasing order)
galoiscyclotomic ξ ≔ (unitgroup ξ)
cyclotomicfactors ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ cyclotomicfactors(p, n): the irreducible factors of the cyclotomic polynomial Φₙ over GF(p) (p ∤ n): φ(n)/ord_n(p) factors, all of degree ord_n(p) — the order of the Frobenius of p in Gal(ℚ(ζₙ)/ℚ); sorted
cyclotomicfactors ξ η ≔ (⫶ ◀ (▶ (fpfactor ξ (cyclotomic η))))
gfgalois ∶ 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the Galois group Gal(GF(pⁿ)/GF(p)) as a permutation group of the elements of gfelements(F) (the points are positions in that list): the cyclic group of order n generated by the Frobenius a ↦ aᵖ
gfgalois ξ ≔ ((es ↦ (generate (∷ (⫶ (e ↦ (hd (filter (k ↦ (eqlist ≐ (nth es k) (gffrob ξ e))) (⍳ (ℓ es))))) es) ⊥))) (gfelements ξ))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 2. Frobenius (Dedekind): for a prime p not dividing the leading coefficient and the discriminant, the degrees of the irreducible factors of f
⍝ modulo p are the cycle lengths of the Frobenius element of the Galois group of f acting on the roots
isgoodprime ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ → 𝔹      ⍝ isgoodprime(f, p): p is a prime that divides neither the leading coefficient nor the discriminant of f (f ∈ ℤ[x] of degree ≥ 1): the factorisation mod p is then square-free and describes the Frobenius element
isgoodprime ξ η ≔ (∧ (isprime η) (∧ (¬ (≐ (mod (last ξ) η) 0)) (¬ (≐ (mod (discriminant ξ) η) 0))))
frobeniuspattern ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ frobeniuspattern(f, p): the degrees of the irreducible factors of f modulo p, with multiplicity, ascending — the cycle type of the Frobenius at p when p is a good prime
frobeniuspattern ξ η ≔ (sort (concat (⫶ (gm ↦ (replicate (▶ gm) (fpdegree (◀ gm)))) (▶ (fpfactor η ξ)))))
⍝ the distinct patterns, sorted lexicographically (by the length first)
pin_gl ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)
pin_gl θ ξ ≔ (ξ (h t ↦ ((cm_fd θ h) (∷ θ ξ) ξ (∷ h (pin_gl θ t)))) (∷ θ ⊥))
frobeniuscensus ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ frobeniuscensus(f, B): the distinct cycle types met by the Frobenius elements at the good primes p ≤ B, sorted. Every pattern listed is the cycle type of an element of the Galois group; by Chebotarev's density theorem every type of the group occurs for a positive proportion of primes (a lower bound for the group, and an upper bound on the elements: the pattern of a good prime is never outside the group)
frobeniuscensus ξ η ≔ (foldr pin_gl ⊥ (⫶ (p ↦ (frobeniuspattern ξ p)) (filter (p ↦ (isgoodprime ξ p)) (primes η))))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 3. criteria
eisensteinprime ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ a prime p for which Eisenstein's criterion applies to the integer polynomial f (p divides every coefficient but the leading one, p ∤ the leading coefficient, p² ∤ the constant term), so that f is irreducible over ℚ; 0 if there is none (the polynomial may still be irreducible)
eisensteinprime ξ ≔ ((g ↦ ((∨ (≺ (ℓ ξ) 1100) (≐ g 0)) 0 ((Π ↦ ((∅ Π) 0 (hd Π))) (filter (p ↦ (∧ (¬ (≐ (mod (last ξ) p) 0)) (¬ (≐ (mod (hd ξ) (⊠ p p)) 0)))) (primefactors g))))) (gcdlist (reverse (⌄ (reverse ξ)))))
iseisenstein ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ does Eisenstein's criterion apply for some prime?
iseisenstein ξ ≔ (¬ (≐ (eisensteinprime ξ) 0))
isdiscsquare ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔹      ⍝ is the discriminant of f a square of a rational number? (then the Galois group of f is contained in the alternating group Aₙ; false when the discriminant is 0 or negative)
isdiscsquare ξ ≔ (sqq_gl (discriminant ξ))
sqq_gl ∶ ℚ → 𝔹
sqq_gl ξ ≔ ((q ↦ (∧ (⩾ q 0) (issquare (⊠ (numer q) (denom q))))) (⊜ ξ))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 4. Galois groups of polynomials of degree ≤ 4 over ℚ (the classical resolvent criteria; Kappe–Warren for D₄ against C₄)
resolventcubic ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ      ⍝ the resolvent cubic of a quartic: for the monic x⁴ + a x³ + b x² + c x + d it is y³ − b y² + (ac − 4d) y − (a²d − 4bd + c²), whose roots are α₁α₂ + α₃α₄, α₁α₃ + α₂α₄, α₁α₄ + α₂α₃ and which has the same discriminant as the quartic; [] unless the degree is 4
resolventcubic ξ ≔ ((f ↦ ((≐ (deg f) 111010000) ((a b c d ↦ (∷ (⊖ (⊞ (⊟ (⊠ (⊠ a a) d) (⊠ 111010000 (⊠ b d))) (⊠ c c))) (∷ (⊟ (⊠ a c) (⊠ 111010000 d)) (∷ (⊖ b) (∷ 1 ⊥))))) (nth f 1101) (nth f 1100) (nth f 1) (nth f 0)) ⊥)) (polymonic ξ))
⍝ the rational roots of a squarefree polynomial
rr_gl ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ
rr_gl ξ ≔ (⫶ (g ↦ (÷ (⊖ (hd g)) (last g))) (filter (g ↦ (≐ (deg g) 1)) (⫶ ◀ (▶ (polyfactor ξ)))))
⍝ does the monic quadratic x² + u x + v split over ℚ(√Δ)?  Its discriminant D must be a rational square, or Δ times one
spl_gl ∶ ℚ → ℚ → ℚ → 𝔹
spl_gl Δ u v ≔ ((D ↦ (∨ (sqq_gl D) (sqq_gl (⊠ Δ D)))) (⊟ (⊠ u u) (⊠ 111010000 v)))
⍝ the group of an irreducible monic quartic, as a code: 1 S₄, 2 A₄, 3 V₄, 4 D₄, 5 C₄
q4_gl ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℕ
q4_gl ξ ≔ ((Δ ↦ ((ρ ↦ ((≐ (ℓ ρ) 0) ((sqq_gl Δ) 1100 1) ((≐ (ℓ ρ) 1) ((r ↦ ((∧ (spl_gl Δ (⊖ r) (nth ξ 0)) (spl_gl Δ (nth ξ 1101) (⊟ (nth ξ 1100) r))) 111010001 111010000)) (hd ρ)) 1101))) (rr_gl (resolventcubic ξ)))) (discriminant ξ))
⍝ the codes of the groups: 0 trivial, 1 S₄, 2 A₄, 3 V₄ (transitive), 4 D₄, 5 C₄, 6 S₃, 7 C₃, 8 C₂, 9 V₄ acting as C₂ × C₂ on two pairs of roots, 10 C₂ acting on two pairs
⍝ at once; -1 outside the cases handled.  Their generators as strings: a generator is its cycles, separated by |, each cycle a string of digits.
tab_gl ∶ ℤ → 𝔏 𝕊
tab_gl ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 1) (∷ "0123" (∷ "01" ⊥)) ((≐ ξ 1100) (∷ "012" (∷ "01|23" ⊥)) ((≐ ξ 1101) (∷ "01|23" (∷ "02|13" ⊥)) ((≐ ξ 111010000) (∷ "0123" (∷ "02" ⊥)) ((≐ ξ 111010001) (∷ "0123" ⊥) ((≐ ξ 111011100) (∷ "012" (∷ "01" ⊥)) ((≐ ξ 111011101) (∷ "012" ⊥) ((≐ ξ 111000000) (∷ "01" ⊥) ((≐ ξ 111000001) (∷ "01" (∷ "23" ⊥)) ((≐ ξ 111001100) (∷ "01|23" ⊥) ⊥))))))))))
spt_gl ∶ 𝕊 → 𝔏 𝕊
spt_gl ξ ≔ (foldr (c acc ↦ ((≐ c '|') (∷ ⊥ acc) (∷ (∷ c (hd acc)) (⌄ acc)))) (∷ ⊥ ⊥) ξ)
perm_gl ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝕊 → 𝔏 ℕ
perm_gl ν ο ξ ≔ (fromcycles ν (⫶ (cy ↦ (⫶ (c ↦ (⊞ ο (⊟ (ord c) (ord '0')))) cy)) (spt_gl ξ)))
⍝ the classification of a squarefree polynomial: (code, (number of points, offset of the first non-linear block))
cl_gl ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔓 ℤ (𝔓 ℕ ℕ)
cl_gl ξ ≔ ((fs ↦ ((nl ↦ ((d ο ↦ (⊗ ((≐ (ℓ nl) 0) 0 ((≐ (ℓ nl) 1) ((g ↦ ((≐ (deg g) 1100) 111000000 ((≐ (deg g) 1101) ((isdiscsquare g) 111011101 111011100) ((≐ (deg g) 111010000) (q4_gl (polymonic g)) 11101)))) (hd nl)) ((∧ (≐ (ℓ nl) 1100) (∧ (≐ (deg (hd nl)) 1100) (≐ (deg (hd (⌄ nl))) 1100))) ((sqq_gl (⊠ (discriminant (hd nl)) (discriminant (hd (⌄ nl))))) 111001100 111000001) 11101))) (⊗ d ο))) (sum_gl (⫶ deg fs)) (sum_gl (⫶ deg (filter (g ↦ (≐ (deg g) 1)) fs))))) (filter (g ↦ (≺ 1 (deg g))) fs))) (srt_gl (⫶ ◀ (▶ (polyfactor (sqfree ξ))))))
sum_gl ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ
sum_gl ξ ≔ (foldl ⊞ 0 ξ)
srt_gl ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)
srt_gl ξ ≔ (foldr (g acc ↦ (isg_gl g acc)) ⊥ ξ)
isg_gl ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℚ)
isg_gl g ξ ≔ (ξ (h t ↦ ((⩽ (deg g) (deg h)) (∷ g ξ) (∷ h (isg_gl g t)))) (∷ g ⊥))
galoisgroup ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the Galois group of the splitting field of f over ℚ (f of degree ≤ 4; repeated roots are ignored) as a permutation group of its roots, up to relabelling of the roots: S₄, A₄, V₄, D₄, C₄ for an irreducible quartic (discriminant and resolvent cubic; D₄ against C₄ by Kappe–Warren), S₃ or C₃ for an irreducible cubic, C₂ for a quadratic, and for a reducible polynomial the group of the product of its factors (two quadratics with the same quadratic field give C₂, otherwise V₄ = C₂ × C₂); [] for degree ≥ 5 and for the zero polynomial
galoisgroup ξ ≔ ((c ↦ ((≐ (◀ c) 11101) ⊥ ((ν ο ↦ (generate ((∅ (tab_gl (◀ c))) (∷ (pid ν) ⊥) (⫶ (perm_gl ν ο) (tab_gl (◀ c)))))) (◀ (▶ c)) (▶ (▶ c))))) (cl_gl ξ))
nm_gl ∶ ℤ → 𝕊
nm_gl ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) "1" ((≐ ξ 1) "S4" ((≐ ξ 1100) "A4" ((≐ ξ 1101) "V4" ((≐ ξ 111010000) "D4" ((≐ ξ 111010001) "C4" ((≐ ξ 111011100) "S3" ((≐ ξ 111011101) "C3" ((≐ ξ 111000000) "C2" ((≐ ξ 111000001) "V4" ((≐ ξ 111001100) "C2" ⊥)))))))))))
or_gl ∶ ℤ → ℕ
or_gl ξ ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) 1 ((≐ ξ 1) 110011000000 ((≐ ξ 1100) 100010000 ((≐ ξ 1101) 111010000 ((≐ ξ 111010000) 111000000 ((≐ ξ 111010001) 111010000 ((≐ ξ 111011100) 111011100 ((≐ ξ 111011101) 1101 ((≐ ξ 111000000) 1100 ((≐ ξ 111000001) 111010000 ((≐ ξ 111001100) 1100 0)))))))))))
galoisname ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝕊      ⍝ the isomorphism type of the Galois group of f (degree ≤ 4): "1", "C2", "C3", "S3", "V4" (the Klein four-group), "C4", "D4" (the dihedral group of order 8), "A4", "S4"; "" outside the cases handled
galoisname ξ ≔ (nm_gl (◀ (cl_gl ξ)))
galoisorder ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℕ      ⍝ the order of the Galois group of f (degree ≤ 4) — the degree [K : ℚ] of the splitting field K of f over ℚ; 0 outside the cases handled
galoisorder ξ ≔ (or_gl (◀ (cl_gl ξ)))
intermediatefielddegrees ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the degrees [F : ℚ] of the intermediate fields ℚ ⊆ F ⊆ K of the splitting field K of f (degree ≤ 4), one for each subgroup H of the Galois group G (the Galois correspondence: [F : ℚ] = |G|/|H|), ascending
intermediatefielddegrees ξ ≔ ((g ↦ (sort (⫶ (h ↦ (div (grouporder g) (grouporder h))) (subgroups g)))) (galoisgroup ξ))
